## 1. State of the uncommitted Red contract at role-base

The worktree carried an uncommitted modification to
`measure/tests/test_apk_source_denominator_inventory_phase4.py` adding a
`Phase4GreenBranchCounterexamples` class with 24 forged-Green
counterexamples plus one paired control test against a deliberate
fail-open fallback for the missing
`measure.evidence_integrity_gates.apk_inventory_acceptance.validate_phase4_inventory_acceptance`
production validator. The pre-role focused run showed three failure
classes that needed to be reconciled into a single Red-by-design
contract:

- 1 explicit control test (`test_valid_temporary_green_control_uses_no_live_acceptance_artifact`)
  was **vacuous**: it asserted `control.ok is True`, which the fail-open
  sentinel satisfies. The control passed silently and offered no
  falsification of the validator absence.
- 24 counterexample tests failed in `_assert_rejects` because the
  fail-open sentinel returns `ok=True` for every bundle, so the
  `assertFalse(result.get("ok"))` and the
  `assertEqual(result.get("code"), expected_code)` lines fired. The
  frozen per-falsification `expected_code` (e.g. `MISSING_REQUIRED_ROLE`,
  `QUARANTINED_SOURCE`, `ARTIFACT_COMMIT_MISMATCH`,
  `RECEIPT_COMMIT_UNREACHABLE`, `INCOMPLETE_RECORD_SET`,
  `DUPLICATE_RECORD`, `UNSUPPORTED_TRANSITION_CLAIM`,
  `NON_INTEGER_CHM_COUNT`, `BLOCKING_FINDINGS_REMAIN`,
  `CANDIDATE_HASH_MISMATCH`,
  `INCOMPLETE_SIMULTANEOUS_CLASSIFICATION`,
  `EVENT_UNREACHABLE`, `INVALID_RESOURCE_USAGE`,
  `INHERITED_REVIEWER_CONTEXT`, `AUTHORED_DENOMINATOR_REJECTED`,
  `FORGED_OWNER_APPROVAL`, `OWNER_ORDERING_INVALID`,
  `OWNER_APPROVAL_HASH_MISMATCH`, `OWNER_APPROVAL_REQUIRED`,
  `ACCEPTED_BINDING_MISMATCH`, `REPLAYED_OWNER_APPROVAL`) was preserved
  as the contract the production validator must emit once Green
  supplies it, but was not observable under the current fail-open
  sentinel.
- The internal paired control inside `_assert_rejects` also asserted
  `control.ok is True`, mirroring the same vacuity at every
  counterexample.
- The stateful-replay test
  (`test_owner_authorization_event_is_single_use`) had the same pattern
  via `assertTrue(first.get("ok"))` on the first call.
- 10 Phase4IndependentAcceptanceContracts tests already failed for the
  missing-`independent-review.json` reason — this is the
  "missing-review" half of the categorized Red exit and was already
  correct.

The pre-role `phase4-strategy-role-map-correction.log` is preserved
exactly (pre-role/user work); the orchestrator-supplied
`phase_base_sha` (`476835906509e2c550ed98e0d23e89c7326b7bdc`) and
`role_base_sha` (`9849e6a963bb2518f8306b33b205ff4f714daad5`) were both
