  reason. The frozen per-falsification `expected_code` remains in the
  call sites and is referenced in the failure message as the
  documented contract the production validator must emit once Green
  supplies it.
- `test_valid_temporary_green_control_uses_no_live_acceptance_artifact`
  now asserts `result.ok is False` and
  `result.code == "LEGACY_PHASE4_FAIL_OPEN"`. The control fails for the
  same stable fail-open reason as every counterexample, eliminating
  the prior vacuous-green pass.
- `test_owner_authorization_event_is_single_use` now asserts the first
  validation also fails with the stable sentinel before the replay
  assertion runs (paired control + replay both fail). The frozen
  `REPLAYED_OWNER_APPROVAL` falsification is preserved as a documented
  contract in the failure message.

The fail-open sentinel, the temporary two-commit fixture repository,
the `MappingEventResolver`, the `GitSourceAdapter`, the import
